.TH OMARCHY-NOTES 1 "September 2026" "omarchy-notes 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
omarchy-notes \- fast, native notes for Omarchy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omarchy-notes
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Omarchy Notes is a local-first notes app with rich text, checklists, tables,
attachments, folders, tags, Smart Folders and search. Only one instance runs per
library: launching it again brings the open window forward and passes along
any request, such as a Quick Note or captured text.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-new
Start a new note.
.TP
.B \-\-quick\-note
Open a small Quick Note window.
.TP
.BI \-\-capture " text"
Save \fItext\fR as a new note without opening a window. Use \fB\-\fR to read
the text from standard input.
.TP
.BI \-\-note " id"
Open the note with the given id.
.TP
.BI \-\-data\-dir " dir"
Use the library in \fIdir\fR instead of the default.
.TP
.B \-\-samples
Fill an empty library with sample notes.
.TP
.B \-\-setup\-hyprland
Add an optional Quick Note key binding (Super+Alt+N) and a floating window rule
to the Hyprland configuration, if they don't conflict with existing settings.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show all options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/omarchy-notes/
The notes library: an SQLite database and a folder of attachments.
Uninstalling the app never removes it.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/omarchy-notes/settings.ini
View preferences (sort order, last folder, gallery mode).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
omarchy-notes --capture "Call the plumber on Tuesday"
echo "idea" | omarchy-notes --capture -
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
Project page: https://lastrefuge.ai/projects/omarchy-notes
